schemeContent.detailedDescription_md:
The scheme component &amp;quot;Creation and Upgradation of Sports Infrastructure&amp;quot; under the &amp;quot;Khelo India Scheme&amp;quot; is a centrally sponsored initiative implemented by the Department of Sports, Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, Government of India, aimed at creating and upgrading sports infrastructure across the country through financial assistance for modern sports facilities, sports science infrastructure, and sports equipment for eligible entities. It supports both new (Greenfield) and existing (Brownfield) sports infrastructure projects that address critical infrastructure gaps. The scheme promotes inclusive, accessible, environmentally sustainable, and community-oriented sports facilities. Assistance may also be provided for sports science infrastructure and sports equipment based on specific requirements and recommendations.
